{"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Persistence","externalID":"Persistence","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module"},"abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker(store:)"},{"type":"text","text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":". A segment is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SegmentStore()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps every event type declared with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the program’s modules, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library’s own; ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore(events:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps only the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types it lists. Each record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a CBOR (RFC 8949) map, its event a map of its properties under their names, written through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", part of ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the conformance, and Swift’s synthesized one works too. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"date in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date?]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the seconds since 2001 it stores, so it reads back exactly. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" written through the CBOR package’s own form, in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type of your own or in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"synthesized conformance, reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. Events of other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types, such as one that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by hand without being listed, are delivered in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run but never written, and reported once as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A store doesn’t read the records Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier wrote, in an earlier format:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" deletes their segments and reports each as a corruption.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each drop is reported on ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": the oldest segments","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at another ","type":"text"},{"code":"schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set. Call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"code":"DatabaseStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"GRDBPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var pl